1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,101
Dinner is three hours away, and your kitchen is already losing control.

2
00:00:04,061 --> 00:00:06,348
Orders are coming in across two brands.

3
00:00:06,348 --> 00:00:09,122
But Manoj, your Chinese cook, is on leave.

4
00:00:09,122 --> 00:00:13,461
Kitchen Shift connects orders, stock, market hours, and your team's availability.

5
00:00:13,461 --> 00:00:17,104
It builds a buying list and a prep plan Asha can actually deliver.

6
00:00:17,104 --> 00:00:20,722
Then Ravi messages the group: Main Market is out of green chillies.

7
00:00:20,722 --> 00:00:25,322
The agent checks another market, asks Ravi to confirm stock, and recalculates.

8
00:00:25,322 --> 00:00:30,626
The emergency trip costs eighteen hundred rupees, so forecast demand alone cannot justify it.

9
00:00:30,626 --> 00:00:34,583
Then Ravi confirms stock and eighteen paneer bowl orders for dinner.

10
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:37,539
Fulfilling those confirmed orders changes the decision.

11
00:00:37,539 --> 00:00:41,122
Neha reviews the costs and approves inside the same Switch thread.

12
00:00:41,122 --> 00:00:44,904
Ravi gets two kilos of paneer and two hundred fifty grams of chillies.

13
00:00:44,904 --> 00:00:48,461
Asha Rao gets eighteen bowls to prep, from five until six.

14
00:00:48,461 --> 00:00:51,600
The menu operator sees exactly which dishes to pause.

15
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,148
One approved version keeps the whole team working from the same plan.

16
00:00:55,148 --> 00:00:59,696
At closing, record what sold, what carried over, and what was discarded.

17
00:00:59,696 --> 00:01:03,557
The workflow runs through Mattermost, Switch, and a real coding agent.

18
00:01:03,557 --> 00:01:07,678
Kitchen Shift helps your team turn daily decisions into a more profitable shift.
